    "body": "Do we really need three types? I don't understand why we can't define equals for lists. I also think that giving \"equivalent\" a normative meaning will be quite awkward as we often use it in notes and such to mean something else.\n\nI also somewhat strongly prefer \"is\" over \"identical\". As it becomes more common having to scan over the long form will be annoying.",
